    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d822">

                <pb facs="0680" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12519a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Silliman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-16T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 16, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Accompany General Carranza until further orders so that we may keep in touch with
                    him through you. Advise Department daily of the program for the day
                    following.</p>
                <p>We have been assured that the new Provisional President, Carbajal, desires to
                    turn over the Government to the Constitutionalists and that no further bloodshed
                    will be necessary.</p>
                <p>Urge Carranza to receive any representative sent by Carbajal and if none are sent
                    advise Carranza to send emissaries to make known to Carbajal the terms upon
                    which transfer of the government may be made. Urge upon Carranza not to allow
                    revenges or cruelties.</p>
                <p>The war would seem to be over and all that remains to be done can be done
                    peacefully and a pacific entrance into Mexico City will greatly aid in assuring
                    friendly intercourse with the outside world.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
